  "articleBody": "When your home needs interior restoration due to an unexpected event, working effectively with your insurance company is key to a smooth process. It often starts with understanding how contractors fit into the picture. You'll want a restoration service that's used to coordinating with adjusters, which means they can present estimates in a clear, claims-friendly format – think line-item pricing, not just a lump sum. Always confirm that the contractor has proper licensing and insurance; this protects you and ensures quality work. Also, don't be afraid to ask about their experience with permits, as some repairs definitely require them, and you don’t want any surprises down the line. The goal is to ensure the scope of work is clearly defined and agreed upon by all parties before permanent repairs begin. We pride ourselves on transparent communication and experience working within the insurance claim framework, helping folks from Colorado Springs up to Boulder get their homes back in shape efficiently and correctly.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}